local-18: draft-only vocabulary for the Qwen4Exp MTP drafter (own patch).

Greedy MTP drafts are scored by a small second head holding only a fixed subset
of the vocabulary (the checkpoint's own INT8 rows + group scales, same Marlin
W8A16 quant method as the target lm_head) instead of the shared 248,320-row
head. The target verifies with the full head, so outputs are unchanged; only
acceptance can drop (a token outside the subset is never drafted).

  VLLM_MTP_DRAFT_VOCAB  unset/0 = off (nothing built, l15 code paths)
                        1       = baked list mtp_draft_vocab_ids.json
                                  (HyperQwen's 40,960 ids, Apache-2.0)
                        /path   = JSON list of ids (or a .pt tensor)
Kept on the full head: draft_sample_method=probabilistic, adaptive
verification, tied embeddings. Ideas from HyperQwen
(qwen3_5-mtp-draft-vocab.patch) and DominikBucko (draft_vocab.py), both
Apache-2.0; no code from miaai (AGPL).

